1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
PlasticWatch is an AI-GIS decision-support tool for PS-08. It turns image reports into verified plastic-waste cleanup priorities.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This prototype uses clearly labelled synthetic reports. The same workflow later accepts citizen images, ward-worker reports, or street-camera frames.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The map merges nearby reports into one hotspot. PH-01 has three reports, 85 percent AI confidence, and lies 35 metres from a drain.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The system explains why it ranked this location: confidence, severity, recurrence, and drain exposure. AI confidence is evidence, not final truth.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Field teams receive a ranked verification queue. This prevents wasted cleanup trips and unsupported responsibility claims.

6
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:22,000
TACO provides training data with 1,500 images and 4,784 labelled objects. It does not perform detection by itself.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
PlasticWatch gives local teams an auditable path from report to verification to cleanup.
